  "note": "full-canvas (1200x1000) pre-built bed of real fries clipped to the interior; draw at 0,0 like the base"
 },
 "notes": "All coordinates normalised to the box-base image (1200x1000); box-lid.webp uses the same canvas and is drawn behind box-base. Sprite w/h are display sizes in box-base pixels (pxPerBoxWidth=1100 = outer width of the box at the front rim); stored files may be up to 2x larger for retina, always draw at w/h. Chicken/onion/pepper are cut from the real griddle photo (real-griddle.jpg) at one scale (median chicken long side = 12% of box width, matched to the real counter photo where chips and chicken share one box; the 6-9% brief figure made chicken look minced next to real fries). Chips are individual real fries cut from real-boxes-counter.jpg; pitta is the real toasted pitta from the same photo. Box base and lid are procedural (Pillow/NumPy). Draw order: lid, base, chips-bed or chips, chips (inside interior, clipped by front rim at rimFrontY), salad (saladZone), chicken/onion/pepper, pitta (pittaAnchor = pitta centre, w = pitta width as a fraction of image width). box-front.webp (front flange + front wall, same canvas) is drawn after the food and before the pitta so food tucks behind the front lip. Darken lower-layer food ~15-20% (multiply) for heap depth."
}